ica so brian  uh what do you think should should they  just raise the standards should they get  rid of them completely because that's  the proposal  uh in briana taylor's home state if you  raise the standard and give  prosecutors officers and judges the  discretion to have no knock warrants or  not  they're going to have no knock warrants  raising the standard doesn't mean  anything  you get rid of them at the end of the  day it's safer for officers it's safer  for  the people inside as well the only  reason why you have no knock warrants is  to ensure that the contraband that's in  the home  isn't secreted away or destroyed and  that is not worth the life of the people  inside or the officers entering  yeah and oftentimes you know there's the  old saying in law school that the minute  you knock you hear a toilet flush  evidence disappears things like that and  that apparently is why we have them  that's one of the legal  theories behind them but so many people  saying get rid of them right now  thanks a lot for joining us here on law  and crime daily we'll see you next time  as we discuss justice  in america  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

